EXT. SKATE PARK - NIGHT

Floodlights. Concrete bowls. Spray paint.

BUDDY ELLISON, 16, in a hoodie, balances on a board at the lip of the bowl. LENA MOREAU, 17, sits on a bench with a sketchbook. SAMIR KHOURY, 15, holds a phone camera, recording.

SAMIR
Do it, Buddy!

BUDDY
Shut up, I'm focusing.

LENA
You're going to break your neck.

BUDDY
Thanks, Lena.

SAMIR
Drop in!

BUDDY
Drop in!

LENA
BUDDY
(speaking at once)
Don't!
(speaking at once)
Watch this!

He drops. The wheels roar down the curve. He rides the wall, flicks the tail, and lands clean. Samir whoops. Lena claps once and returns to her sketchbook.

SAMIR
Did you get it, Buddy?

BUDDY
Did YOU get it?

SAMIR
I think so.

LENA
Let me see.

Samir hands her the phone. She watches. She smiles at the screen. She hands it back.

LENA (CONT'D)
You got it.

Buddy lifts the board over his head like a trophy and screams at the sky.
